## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical mastery of containerized TLS termination, lifecycle upgrades, and host firewall controls in RH9.

## Key Concepts
- Podman/nginx-like TLS termination
- systemd drop-ins for zero-downtime reloads
- nftables rate limiting
- SELinux policy for container access
- certificate rotation with hot reload

## Code Example
```bash
# container run (example)
podman run -d --name proxy \
  -v /srv/certs:/etc/nginx/certs:ro \
  -p 8443:8443:Z nginx:latest
```

```bash
# systemd drop-in (ExecReload for zero downtime)
[Service]
ExecReload=/bin/kill -HUP $MAINPID
```

```bash
# minimal SELinux module (conceptual)
module proxytls 1.0;
require {
  type container_t;
  class file read; class tcp_socket name_bind; 
}
# allow container_t to read certs and bind 8443
allow container_t cert_dir_t:file read;
allow container_t self:tcp_socket name_bind;
```

```bash
# nftables (inbound 8443 and global rate limit)
table inet proxy {
  chain input {
    type filter hook input priority 0;
    tcp dport 8443 accept
  }
}
table inet limit {
  chain input {
    type filter hook input priority 0;
    limit rate 100/minutediffers
  }
}
```

```bash
# test plan (rotation and rollback)
# 1. load test 100 req/min against https://host:8443
# 2. replace files in /srv/certs/rotated with new certs
# 3. touch a trigger or run systemd reload to apply without downtime
# 4. simulate revocation by replacing with old cert and reloading
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses end-to-end TLS termination, dynamic cert provisioning, and zero-downtime reload in a Podman-based RH9 setup. Also tests firewall (nftables), SELinux, and service upgrade discipline.

## Key Concepts
- Podman, nginx as TLS terminator, Vault integration, in-container watcher, systemd upgrades, nftables, SELinux, SNI routing

## Code Example
```nginx
# tls_preread for SNI, per-tenant certs loaded from /etc/nginx/certs
stream {
  map $ssl_preread_server_name $tenant {
    tenantA backendA;
    tenantB backendB;
    tenantC backendC;
  }
  server {
    listen 8443;
    ssl_preread on;
  }
}
```

